Keo founded the Meridian Circle, where neighbors spoke needs aloud and drew repayment routes on clay tablets. Each week, the compass shifted its glow to reflect honesty—bright after a week of open promise, softer when debts lingered, and always returning to a clear beacon when trust endured.

Soon Starling Quay thrived on transparent care: gifts guided paths home, debts acknowledged kept the harbor steady, and every lantern along the quay hummed with the language of mutual shelter, guiding every voyage back to one another.
